// 1. Sample $x_T \sim \mathcal{N}(0, \sigma_{\max}^2 I)$
// 2. For $i = 0, \dots, T-1$:
// 3.   $\hat{x}_0 = D_\theta(x_i/s_i, \sigma_i)$
// 4.   Draw $K$ samples $z_k = \hat{x}_0 + r_t\,\xi_k$, $\xi_k\sim\mathcal{N}$
// 5.   $\bar{g} = \tfrac{1}{K}\sum_k \nabla_{\hat{x}_0}\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{A}(z_k), y)$
// 6.   $g_x = \partial \hat{x}_0/\partial x_i \cdot \bar{g}\;/\;(2\sqrt{\bar\ell})$
// 7.   $x_{i+1} = s\,x_i + f\,\text{score} + \sqrt{f}\,\epsilon - \zeta\,g_x$

// 1. $\mu \leftarrow 0$, init Adam(lr)
// 2. For $t = 0, \dots, T-1$:
// 3.   $\sigma_t, s_t$ from VP schedule; sample $\epsilon \sim \mathcal{N}$
// 4.   $x_t = s_t(\mu + \sigma_t \epsilon)$
// 5.   $\hat\epsilon = (x_t - D_\theta(x_t,\sigma_t))/\sigma_t$
